import csv, json, sqlite3, statistics
from pathlib import Path

root=Path(__file__).parent; db=root/'runtime/server/data.db'
qs=[
('Q01','What is the main purpose of the NIST AI Risk Management Framework?','It helps organizations manage AI risks and promote trustworthy, responsible AI development and use.',6,'the goal of the AI RMF is to offer a resource ... to help manage the many risks of AI and promote trustworthy and responsible development and use'),
('Q02','What are the four core functions of the AI RMF?','Govern, Map, Measure, and Manage.',7,'These functions - GOVERN, MAP, MEASURE, and MANAGE - are broken down further into categories and subcategories.'),
('Q03','What is the purpose of the Govern function?','Govern cultivates a culture of risk management and establishes policies, processes, responsibilities, and oversight across the AI lifecycle.',25,'GOVERN is designed to be a cross-cutting function to inform and be infused throughout the other three functions.'),
('Q04','What is the purpose of the Map function?','Map establishes AI-system context and identifies intended use, stakeholders, impacts, and risks.',28,'The MAP function establishes the context to frame risks related to an AI system.'),
('Q05','What is the purpose of the Measure function?','Measure assesses, analyzes, benchmarks, and monitors AI risks and impacts using appropriate methods.',32,'The MEASURE function employs quantitative, qualitative, or mixed-method tools, techniques, and methodologies.'),
('Q06','What is the purpose of the Manage function?','Manage prioritizes risks and takes actions to respond to, mitigate, or manage them.',35,'The MANAGE function entails allocating resources to the risks mapped and measured and regularly prioritizing them.'),
('Q07','Is the NIST AI RMF mandatory for every organization?','No. It is voluntary.',6,'The Framework is intended to be voluntary, rights-preserving, non-sector-specific, and use-case agnostic.'),
('Q08','Is the AI RMF designed for only one industry?','No. It is non-sector-specific and adaptable across sectors and contexts.',6,'The Framework is intended to be ... non-sector-specific, and use-case agnostic.'),
('Q09','When was AI RMF 1.0 published?','January 2023.',2,'January 2023'),
('Q10','Who is credited as the author of the AI RMF 1.0 publication?','Elham Tabassi.',1,'Elham Tabassi'),
('Q11','What does the framework mean by trustworthy AI characteristics?','They are characteristics used to describe and assess AI-system trustworthiness.',7,'characteristics of trustworthy AI systems include valid and reliable, safe, secure and resilient ...'),
('Q12','Name the trustworthy AI characteristics discussed in the framework.','Valid and reliable; safe; secure and resilient; accountable and transparent; explainable and interpretable; privacy-enhanced; and fair with harmful bias managed.',7,'valid and reliable, safe, secure and resilient, accountable and transparent, explainable and interpretable, privacy enhanced, and fair with harmful biases managed'),
('Q13','Does AI risk management apply only before deployment?','No. It applies throughout the AI lifecycle, including development, deployment, operation, and monitoring.',40,'Test, Evaluation, Verification, and Validation tasks are performed throughout the AI lifecycle.'),
('Q14','What types of methods can be used to measure AI risks?','Quantitative, qualitative, and mixed methods.',32,'The MEASURE function employs quantitative, qualitative, or mixed-method tools, techniques, and methodologies.'),
('Q15','Why is testing important when assessing AI systems?','Testing, evaluation, verification, and validation assess system performance and trustworthiness throughout the lifecycle.',40,'TEVV tasks ... examine the AI system or its components, or detect and remediate problems.'),
('Q16','Why should AI risk measurement methods, metrics, and results be documented?','Documentation supports transparency, accountability, communication, and review of risk assessments and decisions.',32,'Documentation of measurement methods, results, and related decisions supports transparency and accountability.'),
('Q17','Is Govern relevant only at the beginning of the AI lifecycle?','No. Govern is cross-cutting and informs the other functions throughout AI risk management.',7,'GOVERN applies to all stages of organizations’ AI risk management processes and procedures.'),
('Q18','Why can involving different perspectives improve AI risk identification?','Diverse stakeholders can identify assumptions, impacts, risks, and affected groups that a narrow team may miss.',45,'The GOVERN and MAP functions describe the importance of interdisciplinarity and demographically diverse teams.'),
('Q19','What actions can an organization take when an identified AI risk is unacceptable?','It can prioritize and mitigate the risk, reassess or change the system or its use, or decide not to deploy or continue use.',35,'MANAGE function activities include responding to, recovering from, and communicating about incidents and errors.'),
('Q20','How do Govern, Map, Measure, and Manage work together?','Govern provides cross-cutting oversight; Map establishes context; Measure assesses risks; Manage prioritizes and responds.',24,'Functions organize AI risk management activities ... govern, map, measure, and manage AI risks.'),
]
ins=[('Q21','What is the current population of Pune?'),('Q22',"What was Apple's total revenue for its 2025 fiscal year?"),('Q23','Which team won the FIFA World Cup in 2022?'),('Q24','What will the weather be in Pune tomorrow?'),('Q25','What is the current RAM usage of the computer running this application?'),('Q26','What is the current price of a specific laptop?'),('Q27','What AI regulation was announced in India this week?'),('Q28',"What is NVIDIA's current share price?"),('Q29','Who is the principal of my college?'),('Q30','What exact score will my project evaluator award me?')]
dataset=[]
for i,q,a,p,s in qs: dataset.append({'id':i,'question':q,'label':'answerable','reference_answer':a,'supporting_passage':s,'pdf_page':p,'printed_page':p-4 if p>=5 else None})
for i,q in ins: dataset.append({'id':i,'question':q,'label':'insufficient_evidence','reference_answer':'Not available in the indexed document; the system should abstain.','supporting_passage':None,'pdf_page':None,'printed_page':None})
conn=sqlite3.connect(db); conn.row_factory=sqlite3.Row
hist=conn.execute('select question,answer,sources,created_at from chat_history order by id desc').fetchall(); conn.close()
byq={}
for r in hist:
 if r['question'] not in byq: byq[r['question']]=dict(r)
rows=[]
for d in dataset:
 h=byq.get(d['question']); failure=None if h else 'Benchmark request did not produce a persisted response before the 120-second harness timeout.'
 rows.append({**d,'generated_response':h['answer'] if h else '', 'retrieved_evidence':json.loads(h['sources'] or '[]') if h else [], 'latency_ms':None, 'abstained':None, 'technical_failure':failure, 'correctness':'not_scored' if failure else 'manual_review_required', 'unsupported_claim':'not_scored' if failure else 'manual_review_required','citation_assessment':'No PDF page citation emitted by Version 1 API'})
completed=[r for r in rows if not r['technical_failure']]
metrics={'run_status':'incomplete - frozen snapshot after generation timeouts','attempts':30,'completed_responses':len(completed),'technical_failures':30-len(completed),'answer_correctness':{'count':None,'denominator':20,'percentage':None,'note':'Not scored: incomplete run.'},'unsupported_answer_rate':{'count':None,'denominator':len(completed),'percentage':None},'abstention_accuracy':{'count':None,'denominator':10,'percentage':None},'retrieval_recall_at_5':{'count':None,'denominator':20,'percentage':None},'citation_accuracy':{'supported':None,'total':0,'percentage':None,'missing_citations':len(completed)},'performance':{'mean_latency_ms':None,'median_latency_ms':None,'p95_latency_ms':None,'failure_rate_percent':round((30-len(completed))*100/30,1),'memory_usage':'not measured reliably'}}
(root/'evaluation_dataset.json').write_text(json.dumps({'dataset_status':'frozen provisional ground truth; pages refer to PDF pages','questions':dataset},indent=2),encoding='utf8')
(root/'raw_outputs.json').write_text(json.dumps({'run_status':metrics['run_status'],'results':rows},indent=2),encoding='utf8')
(root/'metrics_summary.json').write_text(json.dumps(metrics,indent=2),encoding='utf8')
fields=['id','label','question','reference_answer','generated_response','retrieved_evidence','abstained','latency_ms','technical_failure','correctness','unsupported_claim','citation_assessment']
with (root/'question_results.csv').open('w',newline='',encoding='utf8') as f:
 w=csv.DictWriter(f,fieldnames=fields);w.writeheader();[w.writerow({k:(json.dumps(r[k]) if isinstance(r[k],list) else r[k]) for k in fields}) for r in rows]
(root/'evaluation_report.md').write_text(f'''# Version 1 Offline RAG Evaluation\n\n## Executive summary\n\nThis is a frozen **incomplete** evaluation snapshot. The isolated Version 1 stack ingested NIST.AI.100-1.pdf into 34 Chroma chunks. The benchmark harness used the actual HTTP chat route, Top-K 5, document-only retrieval, and no threshold. It timed out at 120 seconds for most requests, so no correctness, abstention, retrieval-recall, citation-accuracy, or latency aggregate is reported as a measured score.\n\n## Actual architecture\n\nPDF extraction: `pdf-parse`; chunking: sentence-oriented 600-word chunks with 100-word overlap; embeddings: Ollama `qwen3-embedding:0.6b`; vector database: Chroma cosine distance; LLM: Ollama `qwen3:4b`; generation: temperature 0.4 and `num_predict` 1000. No retrieval similarity threshold is active.\n\n## Results\n\nCompleted persisted responses: {len(completed)}/30. Technical failures/timeouts: {30-len(completed)}/30. The API returns source metadata but ingestion does not preserve PDF page metadata, so answer-level page citations are unavailable.\n\n## Limitations and Version 2 recommendations\n\nThis is not a completed baseline. Address generation timeouts, preserve page-level metadata during extraction/chunking, implement evidence-aware abstention before LLM generation, and emit claim-linked citations. Re-run the frozen dataset after those changes only as Version 2, retaining this snapshot unchanged.\n''',encoding='utf8')
(root/'error_analysis.md').write_text(f'''# Error analysis\n\n## Observed failure\n\nThe actual Version 1 `/api/chat` pipeline was invoked with the indexed document. Most requests failed to persist a `done` result within the 120-second harness limit. This is recorded as a technical failure, not an incorrect answer.\n\n## Likely causes\n\n- The application requests up to 1,000 generated tokens for every answer.\n- It sends up to five large chunks to the local model.\n- No request timeout exists in the production generation service.\n- Chunks lack PDF page metadata, so citations cannot be page-validated.\n\n## Counts\n\nPersisted responses: {len(completed)}. Unfinished/timeout attempts: {30-len(completed)}. No unsupported-answer, correctness, or retrieval-recall score is inferred from missing outputs.\n''',encoding='utf8')
print(f'created six deliverables; persisted responses={len(completed)}')
